<title>BELGIUM: EU vets maintain pig trade ban.</title>
<headline>EU vets maintain pig trade ban.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ban on exports of Dutch pigs should stay, European Union experts ruled on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The (EU's Standing Veterinary) Committee has recommended no change. The situation will be reviewed at the next veterinary meeting,&quot; a European Commission official said.</p>
<p>The ban, imposed following an outbreak of swine fever, is now in its third week.</p>
<p>A sixty day ban on movements of pigs affecting four German states also remains in place and following new outbreaks movement of pigs from two Italian regions has been banned by the Italian authorities.</p>
<p>&quot;The Committee were satisfied that the controls already in place are appropriate and that there should be no lifting of the movement orders,&quot; the official added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
